{"title": "<span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Matter and its states</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物质与物质的状态</span>", "slides": [{"id": "c2-states:title", "h": "<div class=\"s-kicker\">🧊 <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Physical Properties of Matter</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物质的物理性质</span></div><h2 class=\"s-title\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Matter and its states</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物质与物质的状态</span></h2><p class=\"s-hook\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Push the plunger of a sealed syringe full of air and it slides in. Fill it with water and it will not budge. That one difference — how closely the particles are packed — explains every row of the states-of-matter table.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">推一支装满空气、封住口的针筒，活塞能推进去；装满水就推不动。就这一个差别——粒子挤得有多紧——解释了物质状态表的每一行。</span></span></p><div class=\"s-diff\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Difficulty</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">难度</span> <b>●○○</b></div><div class=\"s-meta\">⏱ 20 min · ★ <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">essential</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">必会</span></div>"}, {"id": "c2-states:keys", "h": "<div class=\"s-kicker\">🔑 <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Must know</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">必须记住</span> · <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Matter and its states</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物质与物质的状态</span></div><ol class=\"s-list\"><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Matter = has mass + takes up space. 4 states: solid, liquid, gas, plasma.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物质＝有质量＋占空间。4 种状态：固、液、气、等离子体。</span></div></li><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Solid: definite shape and volume. Liquid: indefinite shape, definite volume. Gas: both indefinite.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">固体：形状体积都固定。液体：形状不定、体积固定。气体：都不固定。</span></div></li><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Only gases are compressible (particles far apart).</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">只有气体可压缩（粒子相距远）。</span></div></li></ol><div class=\"s-fig\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 540 245\" class=\"fig wide\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"particles in solid, liquid and gas\"><defs><marker id=\"mvh\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"mvh\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" rx=\"14\" class=\"cbox\"/><text x=\"95.0\" y=\"190\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"ct\"><tspan class=\"en\">SOLID</tspan><tspan class=\"zh\"> 固体</tspan></text><text x=\"95.0\" y=\"206\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"lbl s en\">fixed shape & volume</text><text x=\"95.0\" y=\"221\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"lbl s zh\">形状体积固定</text><circle cx=\"42\" cy=\"150\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"68\" cy=\"150\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"94\" cy=\"150\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"150\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"146\" cy=\"150\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"42\" cy=\"124\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"68\" cy=\"124\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"94\" cy=\"124\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"124\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"146\" cy=\"124\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"42\" cy=\"98\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"68\" cy=\"98\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"94\" cy=\"98\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"98\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"146\" cy=\"98\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"42\" cy=\"72\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"68\" cy=\"72\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"94\" cy=\"72\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"72\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"146\" cy=\"72\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><rect x=\"195\" y=\"20\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" rx=\"14\" class=\"cbox\"/><text x=\"270.0\" y=\"190\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"ct\"><tspan class=\"en\">LIQUID</tspan><tspan class=\"zh\"> 液体</tspan></text><text x=\"270.0\" y=\"206\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"lbl s en\">fixed volume, takes shape</text><text x=\"270.0\" y=\"221\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"lbl s zh\">体积固定、形状随容器</text><circle cx=\"249\" cy=\"93\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"288\" cy=\"87\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"274\" cy=\"108\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"218\" cy=\"119\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"219\" cy=\"89\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"261\" cy=\"142\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"285\" cy=\"150\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"326\" cy=\"85\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"312\" cy=\"103\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"248\" cy=\"124\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"305\" cy=\"132\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"214\" cy=\"145\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"311\" cy=\"154\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"327\" cy=\"129\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"237\" cy=\"151\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><circle cx=\"295\" cy=\"114\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><rect x=\"370\" y=\"20\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" rx=\"14\" class=\"cbox\"/><text x=\"445.0\" y=\"190\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"ct\"><tspan class=\"en\">GAS</tspan><tspan class=\"zh\"> 气体</tspan></text><text x=\"445.0\" y=\"206\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"lbl s en\">fills the container</text><text x=\"445.0\" y=\"221\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"lbl s zh\">充满容器</text><circle cx=\"415\" cy=\"86\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><line x1=\"406\" y1=\"95\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"108\" class=\"mv\" marker-end=\"url(#mvh)\"/><circle cx=\"459\" cy=\"115\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><line x1=\"463\" y1=\"127\" x2=\"469\" y2=\"143\" class=\"mv\" marker-end=\"url(#mvh)\"/><circle cx=\"464\" cy=\"52\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><line x1=\"462\" y1=\"39\" x2=\"460\" y2=\"22\" class=\"mv\" marker-end=\"url(#mvh)\"/><circle cx=\"405\" cy=\"139\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><line x1=\"409\" y1=\"151\" x2=\"414\" y2=\"168\" class=\"mv\" marker-end=\"url(#mvh)\"/><circle cx=\"499\" cy=\"104\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><line x1=\"512\" y1=\"105\" x2=\"529\" y2=\"106\" class=\"mv\" marker-end=\"url(#mvh)\"/><circle cx=\"395\" cy=\"50\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><line x1=\"406\" y1=\"42\" x2=\"420\" y2=\"32\" class=\"mv\" marker-end=\"url(#mvh)\"/><circle cx=\"487\" cy=\"152\" r=\"11\" class=\"pa\"/><line x1=\"475\" y1=\"158\" x2=\"460\" y2=\"165\" class=\"mv\" marker-end=\"url(#mvh)\"/></svg></div>"}, {"id": "c2-states:fig0", "h": "<div class=\"s-kicker\">🖼️ <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Picture it</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">看图理解</span> · <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Matter and its states</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物质与物质的状态</span></div><div class=\"s-fig\"><div class=\"mtree\"><ul><li><span class=\"tn d0\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Matter (has mass, takes up space)</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物质（有质量、占空间）</span></span></span><ul><li><span class=\"tn d1\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Solid</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">固体</span></span><span class=\"tn-note\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">definite shape · definite volume · not compressible</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">定形 · 定体积 · 不可压缩</span></span></span></span></li><li><span class=\"tn d1\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Liquid</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">液体</span></span><span class=\"tn-note\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">takes container shape · definite volume · not compressible</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">随容器变形 · 定体积 · 不可压缩</span></span></span></span></li><li><span class=\"tn d1\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Gas</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">气体</span></span><span class=\"tn-note\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">no fixed shape or volume · compressible</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">形状体积都不定 · 可压缩</span></span></span></span></li><li><span class=\"tn d1\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Plasma</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">等离子体</span></span><span class=\"tn-note\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">very hot, charged gas (lightning, stars)</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">极热的带电气体（闪电、恒星）</span></span></span></span></li></ul></li></ul></div></div>"}, {"id": "c2-states:hard", "h": "<div class=\"s-kicker hard\">🧗 <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">The hard part</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">难点</span> · <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Matter and its states</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物质与物质的状态</span></div><h3 class=\"s-h\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Linking particles to the property table</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">把粒子和性质表联系起来</span></span></h3><p class=\"s-why\"><span class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Students memorise the table but cannot explain it.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">学生背得出表，却解释不了。</span></span></p><ol class=\"s-steps\"><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Tight + fixed in place → keeps shape and volume (solid).</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">紧密＋位置固定→保持形状和体积（固体）。</span></div></li><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Touching but sliding → flows (shape changes), volume fixed (liquid).</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">接触但能滑动→能流动（形状变），体积固定（液体）。</span></div></li><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Far apart → fills container, compressible (gas).</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">相距远→充满容器、可压缩（气体）。</span></div></li></ol><div class=\"s-try\"><b><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Try</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">试一试</span></b> <div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Why does a liquid take the shape of its container?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">液体为什么会变成容器的形状？</span></div><details><summary><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Answer</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">答案</span></summary><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Its particles are touching but can slide past one another, so it flows.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">它的粒子相互接触但能彼此滑动，所以能流动。</span></div></details></div>"}, {"id": "c2-states:traps", "h": "<div class=\"s-kicker trap\">⚠️ <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Traps &amp; tip</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">陷阱与提示</span> · <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Matter and its states</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物质与物质的状态</span></div><ul class=\"s-list traps\"><li><div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Liquid has indefinite volume → it is the shape that changes; volume is definite.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">液体体积不固定 → 变的是形状，体积固定。</span></div></li></ul><div class=\"s-tnote\">🟡 <div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Your class notes list 4 common states including plasma, and say liquids are not compressible. Many textbooks list only 3 everyday states and say liquids are \"nearly\" incompressible. On this test: 4 states, and only gases are compressible.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">课堂讲义列出包括等离子体在内的 4 种常见状态，并说液体不可压缩。很多教材只列 3 种日常状态，说液体「几乎」不可压缩。考试按讲义：4 种状态，只有气体可压缩。</span></div></div><div class=\"s-tip\">🎯 <div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Picture each in a jar: keeps shape? fills the jar?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">想象放进罐子：保持形状吗？充满罐子吗？</span></div></div>"}], "cards": [{"id": "c2-states.c0", "f": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Definition of matter?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物质的定义？</span></div>", "b": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Anything with mass that takes up space (volume).</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">有质量并占据空间（体积）的任何东西。</span></div>"}, {"id": "c2-states.c1", "f": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">The 4 common states?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">4 种常见状态？</span></div>", "b": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Solid, liquid, gas, plasma.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">固体、液体、气体、等离子体。</span></div>"}, {"id": "c2-states.c2", "f": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Which state is compressible?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">哪种状态可压缩？</span></div>", "b": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Gas only — its particles are far apart.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">只有气体——粒子相距很远。</span></div>"}, {"id": "c2-states.c3", "f": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Liquid: shape and volume?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">液体：形状和体积？</span></div>", "b": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Indefinite shape (takes the container's shape), definite volume.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">形状不固定（随容器），体积固定。</span></div>"}, {"id": "c2-states.c4", "f": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">How do liquid particles move?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">液体粒子怎么运动？</span></div>", "b": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">They stay in close contact but slide past one another.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">紧挨在一起，但能彼此滑动。</span></div>"}], "quiz": [{"id": "c2-states.p1", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Which state has a definite volume but takes the shape of its container?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">哪种状态体积固定，但形状随容器改变？</span></div>", "opts": null, "a": null, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Think of milk poured into a glass.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">想象把牛奶倒进杯子。</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Liquid</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">液体</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Liquids keep their volume but flow into the container's shape.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">液体保持体积，但会流成容器的形状。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c2-states.p2", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Name the fourth common state of matter (besides solid, liquid, gas).</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">说出物质的第四种常见状态（固、液、气之外）。</span></div>", "opts": null, "a": null, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Found in lightning and stars.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">闪电和恒星里有它。</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Plasma</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">等离子体</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">The 4 common states: solid, liquid, gas, plasma.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">4 种常见状态：固体、液体、气体、等离子体。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c2-states.p3", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Is the light from a flashlight matter?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">手电筒发出的光是物质吗？</span></div>", "opts": ["<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Yes, because you can see it</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">是，因为看得见</span></span>", "<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Yes, because it fills the room</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">是，因为它充满房间</span></span>", "<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">No, because it has no mass and takes up no space</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">不是，因为它没有质量、不占空间</span></span>", "<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">No, because it is not a solid</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">不是，因为它不是固体</span></span>"], "a": 2, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Matter needs mass AND volume.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">物质要同时有质量和体积。</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">No — light is energy: no mass, no volume.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">不是——光是能量：无质量、不占体积。</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Light has no mass and does not take up space → energy, not matter.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">光没有质量也不占空间→是能量，不是物质。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c2-states.p4", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">In a particle picture, the particles are close together but arranged randomly, with no regular pattern. Which state?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">粒子示意图中，粒子挨得很近但排列杂乱、没有规则。是哪种状态？</span></div>", "opts": null, "a": null, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Close together rules out gas. Regular pattern would be solid.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">挨得近排除气体；排列规则才是固体。</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Liquid</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">液体</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Close together → solid or liquid. Random arrangement → liquid.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">挨得近→固体或液体。排列杂乱→液体。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c2-states.p5", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Which state(s) are NOT compressible according to your notes?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">按讲义，哪些状态不可压缩？</span></div>", "opts": ["<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Gas only</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">只有气体</span></span>", "<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Solid and liquid</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">固体和液体</span></span>", "<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Liquid and gas</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">液体和气体</span></span>", "<span class=\"bi chbi\"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">All three</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">三种都是</span></span>"], "a": 1, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Which state is the only compressible one?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">唯一可压缩的是哪种？</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Solid and liquid</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">固体和液体</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Gases are compressible; solids and liquids are not.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">气体可压缩；固体和液体不可压缩。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c2-states.p6", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">A 500 mL bottle holds 300 mL of water and the rest is air. Water is poured into a 1 L jug, and the air escapes into the room. What is the new volume of the water, and what happens to the volume of the air? Explain.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">一个 500 mL 瓶子里有 300 mL 水，其余是空气。把水倒进 1 L 的壶里，空气散到房间中。水的体积现在是多少？空气的体积怎样变化？说明理由。</span></div>", "opts": null, "a": null, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Which state has a definite volume?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">哪种状态体积固定？</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Water: still 300 mL (definite volume). Air: spreads out to fill the room, so its volume increases (indefinite volume).</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">水：仍是 300 mL（体积固定）。空气：扩散充满房间，体积变大（体积不固定）。</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Liquid → definite volume → 300 mL in the jug, only the shape changes.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">液体→体积固定→壶里仍是 300 mL，只是形状变了。</span></div>", "whys": null}, {"id": "c2-states.p7", "q": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">A scuba tank holds enough air to fill a whole room, yet the tank is small. A tank this size could never hold a room's worth of water. Explain both facts using the particle model.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">一个潜水气瓶装的空气能充满整个房间，可气瓶却很小。同样大小的瓶子绝不可能装下一房间的水。用粒子模型解释这两个事实。</span></div>", "opts": null, "a": null, "hint": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Which state is compressible, and why?</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">哪种状态可压缩，为什么？</span></div>", "ans": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Gas particles are far apart, so air can be compressed into the small tank and expands to fill a room when released. Water particles already touch, so water cannot be compressed — a room's worth of water keeps its large volume.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">气体粒子相距很远，空气能被压进小瓶，放出时又膨胀充满房间。水分子已经紧挨着，水不能被压缩——一房间的水体积还是那么大。</span></div>", "why": "<div class=\"bi \"><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Gas: lots of space between particles → squeezed into the tank.</span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">气体：粒子间空隙大→可压进气瓶。</span></div>", "whys": null}], "v": 1, "key": "topic-c2-states"}